#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "8559e2bf-8b48-5e26-81c6-0db03d93645a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5451" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis $\\{\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ of the Euclidean plane $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as depicted below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/867/Source/Images/a075449f9d98c2f5b4e14b915f2365f2.png)\n\nWe can find the images of $\\{\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ni^{′} &= T(i) = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} = i \\\\\nj^{′} &= T(j) = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} =-j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/867/Source/Images/45b1b054a2d140d9a815f9b4816138e7.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents the reflection across the $x$-axis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/id #uuid "ef17b637-7c4d-5515-99b7-13b1290244f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-5452" :question/problem "A linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ represents a dilation. Given that $\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$ what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$?" :question/worked-solution "We can write $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(v) &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}v\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\mathbf{v}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ is a dilation with scale factor\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nRemember that the matrix representing a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "892c68cb-26fd-5950-89aa-95af200ef566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086749} {:answer/id #uuid "dc390f5f-54e3-5dbe-a1d8-9c5cebeebd6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086750} {:answer/id #uuid "472454e6-6141-5a63-9f61-ce5b4c149f65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086751} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcc7404-55cb-5603-9405-272b2d821e08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086752} {:answer/id #uuid "77a41bcf-dcc5-5714-b8fd-ca53ea1a599a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc390f5f-54e3-5dbe-a1d8-9c5cebeebd6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086750} :answer-field/id #uuid "767f5b44-4e93-5075-ae32-e55eb00505c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086748}] :question/id #uuid "cad47c40-27a1-5f31-8c6f-6a66b9bee47d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78299" :question/problem "Which of the following represents a reflection across the $y$-axis?"}]}
